摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Lazy MCP gateway for DeepSeek Harness: one stable proxy tool instead of N tool schemas, servers connect on first use and idle out, metadata cached to disk.","id":"gh:1365064934","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-mcp-lazy","slug":"wings1848/dsh-mcp-lazy","topics":["deepseek","dsh","dsh-plugin","llm","mcp","model-context-protocol","tokens"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Lazy MCP gateway for DeepSeek Harness: one stable proxy tool instead of N tool schemas, servers conn"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ect on first use and idle out, metadata cached to disk."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-mcp-lazy"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A lazy MCP gateway for DeepSeek Harness. It puts **one**\ntool in front of the model instead of N MCP"},{"id":"p3s2","text":" tool schemas: servers start on first use, idle\nout again, and their tool metadata is cached on disk"},{"id":"p3s3","text":" so `search` and `describe` never spawn\nanything."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## Why"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"`@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` connects every configured server at startup and registers every\none of"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" its tools as a native tool. As its own README puts it, tool descriptions and input\nschemas \"enter e"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"very request while the tools are registered\". A handful of servers therefore\ncosts thousands of toke"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"ns on every request and one resident child process each — whether or\nnot the model ever calls them."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"This plugin keeps the model-facing surface at exactly one tool whose schema never changes,\ndiscovers"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" tools on demand from a disk cache, and only spawns a server when a call needs it."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## The numbers"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Measured against `chrome-devtools-mcp@1.6.0` (29 tools), both sides rendered the same way —\nJSON byt"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"es of the tool definitions, then four bytes per token:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| | per request |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| native registration | 21252 bytes ≈ **5313 tokens** |\n| this gateway | 1525 bytes ≈ **381 tokens**"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" |\n| saved | **92.8%** |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The gateway figure is constant: configuring ten more servers does not move it, because their\nschemas"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" are read on demand rather than sent every request."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**The honest counterweight.** The gateway costs a fixed 1525 bytes, so it wins only when a\nserver's "},{"id":"p12s2","text":"rendered tool definitions exceed that. The bundled fixture offers 7 small tools and\nthe saving drops"},{"id":"p12s3","text":" to 1.7%. A server with a couple of tiny tools would make the gateway a net\nloss. Measure your own b"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"ver with a couple of tiny tools would make the gateway a net\nloss. Measure your own before assuming:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Works with the DeepSeek Harness `0.1.5-rc` and `0.2.0-rc` lines (verified against\n`0.2.0-rc.2`); the"},{"id":"p16s2","text":" package's peer ranges declare exactly that."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"That installs the package into the profile and registers its bundle patch, which inserts the\n`mcp-la"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"zy` row. Then give it your servers in the profile's `cordis.patch.yml`:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Restart the profile. Every field is documented in docs/configuration.md."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### Moving servers off `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client`"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Every writer of MCP configuration in this ecosystem emits a `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` row:\nthe c"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"onfig-manager panel hardcodes that package name, `@hyzyn/dsh-codegraph` writes a managed\nrow, and a "},{"id":"p21s3","text":"hand-written config follows the same convention. Such a row registers each MCP tool\nas a real tool, "},{"id":"p21s4","text":"so its schemas enter every request — and a server listed in **both** places\ncancels the saving this "},{"id":"p21s5","text":"plugin exists for, with no error and nothing to notice. (The `mcp({})`\nstatus output does warn you —"},{"id":"p21s6","text":" for any server the other plugin serves natively, whether or not\nthis one has it too — which is how "},{"id":"p21s7","text":"you usually find out.)"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"`adopt` does the move for you:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Or, without leaving the session, as a slash command:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"The command drives the same CLI, so the plan, the backups and the write are one code path; a\nsuccess"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"ful `apply` is followed by a re-plan whose result is shown to you, so the answer to \"did\nit work?\" i"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"s evidence rather than an assurance. It still requires the human to type it: nothing\nruns at plugin "},{"id":"p26s4","text":"ce rather than an assurance. It still requires the human to type it: nothing\nruns at plugin startup."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"It reads what is *actually* mounted (`dsh --profile <p> --dump-config`, so all four patch layers\nare"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" composed), marks each original row `disabled: true` **in place**, and appends the server to\nthis pl"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ugin's `servers` list. Nothing else in the file is touched — comments, blank lines and\n`!!js` expres"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"sions are preserved byte for byte — and a row it cannot move safely is reported\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## What the model sees"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"One tool, always the same 11 parameters:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Seven of the 11 are the actions above. The other four shape a `search` and are\nnever needed for anyt"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"he 11 are the actions above. The other four shape a `search` and are\nnever needed for anything else:"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"| Parameter | Meaning | Default | Limit |"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"| `regex` | Treat `search` as a regular expression rather than literal text. | `false` | — |\n| `incl"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"udeSchemas` | Include each match's parameter summary in the result. | `true` | — |\n| `limit` | How m"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"any matches to return. | `12` | `40`; clamped into 1–40, never an error |\n| `offset` | Skip this man"},{"id":"p33s4","text":"y matches, for paging through a long result. | `0` | — |"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"That one tool is the **whole** model-facing surface by default. `directTools` is\nthe opt-in that pro"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"motes chosen server tools into real native tools instead —\nsee docs/configuration.md\nfor what it acc"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"epts, and why the default is the cheap choice."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"The v1 boundary, stated plainly:"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"- **Tools only.** No MCP resources, prompts, sampling, or elicitation. Only `tools/list_changed`\nis "},{"id":"p37s2","text":"subscribed.\n- **No OAuth.** Authentication is a plaintext `headers` entry or an environment variable"},{"id":"p37s3","text":".\n- **Image and audio results are not forwarded.** They are projected to a one-line metadata\nentry ("},{"id":"p37s4","text":"type and byte count). Forwarding pixels needs attachment storage this plugin does\nnot implement.\n- *"},{"id":"p37s5","text":"*No approval gate.** MCP calls follow your DSH permission preset.\n- **No config interop.** It reads "},{"id":"p37s6","text":"DSH-native config only; it will not import `.mcp.json`,\nCursor, Claude Code, Codex, or VS Code serve"},{"id":"p37s7","text":"r lists.\n- **The regex guard is deliberately narrow.** A 256-character cap plus a nested-quantifier\n"},{"id":"p37s8","text":"check, which does **not** catch overlapping alternation like `(a|aa)+` or polynomial\nbacktracking li"},{"id":"p37s9","text":"ke `a*a*a*b`. A full analyser would mean a second runtime dependency.\n- **No SSE or unix-socket tran"},{"id":"p37s10","text":"sports.** `stdio` and `streamable-http` only.\n- **`npx` is not resolved to the underlying binary**, "},{"id":"p37s11","text":"so an `npx`-launched server costs one\nextra Node parent process.\n- **A secret passed through `args` "},{"id":"p37s12","text":"lands in the child's `argv`**, where `ps` and\n`/proc/<pid>/cmdline` can read it. That path exists on"},{"id":"p37s13","text":"ly because some servers accept a token\nno other way; `envFrom` alone keeps the value out of `argv`."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
